<Base lang="en" title="UP Scholarship 2026-27: Verification Running Now — Payment Reported 15–22 December (Renewal) / 24–31 December (Fresh)" description="UP Scholarship 2026-27 forms closed on 13 November — verification is now running: renewal verification by 28 November, fresh verification by 30 November, college forwarding ended 26 November, and payment reported for 15–22 December (renewal) and 24–31 December (fresh). What each stage means and what students should do now." path="/en/blog/up-scholarship-verification-payment-date/" altPath="/blog/up-scholarship-verification-payment-date/" faqs={faqs} updated="28 November 2026" datePublished="2026-11-21" dateModified="2026-11-28">>
<div class="content-col"><h1 class="page-title">UP Scholarship 2026-27: verification is running — payment reported 15–22 December (renewal) / 24–31 December (fresh)</h1>
<p class="updated-line">As per the reported fourth revised timetable (Social Welfare Department, 20 November 2026 · AKTU notice, 25 November 2026) · 28 November 2026 — the portal has published no separate notice</p>
<figure class="blog-featured"><img src="/images/blog/up-scholarship-verification-payment-date-featured.webp" alt="UP Scholarship 2026-27 — verification running and December payment dates (example illustration)" /><figcaption>Example illustration — edistrictupseva.com</figcaption></figure>
<p>The form window for UP Scholarship 2026-27 is over. As per the revised timetable, fresh and renewal applications closed on <strong>13 November 2026</strong>, the final print was due by 15 November and the hard copy had to be submitted to the college by 16 November. The process has now moved fully into verification — and the fourth revised timetable (AKTU notice of 25 November 2026) has moved the payment dates: renewal is reported for <strong>15–22 December</strong> and fresh for <strong>24–31 December</strong>. This article follows our earlier <a href="/en/blog/up-scholarship-verification-november-2026/">November verification schedule</a> and the <a href="/en/blog/up-scholarship-deadline-extension-13-november-2026/">13 November deadline report</a>: it lays out which stage is running today, what happens next, when the money is reported to arrive, and the few things a student should still do so the payment does not get stuck at the last step.</p>
<section class="box"><h2>Where the process stands today — 28 November</h2><p>The last dates of this week belong to renewal. <strong>College forwarding ended on 26 November 2026</strong> — if your form has left the college, it is now in the university stage. <strong>University / affiliating-agency verification is due by 28 November 2026 for renewal</strong> and <strong>by 30 November 2026 for fresh applicants</strong>. AKTU-affiliated colleges must submit the verified student list with the original affidavit by <strong>28 November</strong>. <strong>NIC scrutiny for fresh applicants runs 26 November–8 December 2026</strong> (renewal NIC scrutiny 6–30 November). If your status today shows the form verified at the institute and university level, you do not have to do anything right now — but if it is still sitting with the college, read the action list below today itself, because the forwarding deadline has already passed.</p><figure class="shot"><img src="/images/blog/scholarship-payment-timeline.svg" alt="UP Scholarship 2026-27 — verification to payment timeline (reported fourth revised timetable)" /><figcaption>Verification to payment — reported fourth revised timetable — edistrictupseva.com</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="box"><h2>The full reported timetable — stage by stage</h2><table class="data"><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Who / what</th><th>Reported date</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Applications closed (fresh + renewal)</td><td>Students</td><td>13 November 2026 (completed)</td></tr><tr><td>Final print</td><td>Students</td><td>By 15 November 2026 (completed)</td></tr><tr><td>Hard copy submission</td><td>Students → college</td><td>By 16 November 2026 (completed)</td></tr><tr><td>College forwarding</td><td>College / institute</td><td>Ended 26 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>University / affiliating-agency verification — renewal</td><td>University</td><td>By 28 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>University / affiliating-agency verification — fresh</td><td>University</td><td>By 30 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Aadhaar authentication (PFMS)</td><td>PFMS</td><td>6–21 November 2026 (completed)</td></tr><tr><td>NIC scrutiny — renewal</td><td>NIC</td><td>6–30 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>NIC scrutiny — fresh</td><td>NIC</td><td>26 November – 8 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Fund transfer (payment) — renewal</td><td>PFMS → bank account</td><td>15–22 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Fund transfer (payment) — fresh</td><td>PFMS → bank account</td><td>24–31 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Rectified-application payment — renewal</td><td>PFMS → bank account</td><td>16–25 January 2027</td></tr><tr><td>Rectified-application payment — fresh</td><td>PFMS → bank account</td><td>27–31 January 2027</td></tr></tbody></table><section class="box"><h2>Fresh and renewal — the dates are different (fourth revised timetable, AKTU notice of 25 November 2026)</h2>
<p>The Social Welfare Department's fourth revised timetable of 20 November 2026 has moved the payment dates — these dates are reported from two sources, so check the official portal:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>College forwarding (both categories):</strong> ended 26 November 2026</li>
<li><strong>University verification — renewal:</strong> by 28 November 2026</li>
<li><strong>University verification — fresh:</strong> by 30 November 2026</li>
<li><strong>Fund transfer (payment) — renewal:</strong> 15–22 December 2026</li>
<li><strong>Fund transfer (payment) — fresh:</strong> 24–31 December 2026</li>
<li><strong>NIC scrutiny — fresh:</strong> 26 November – 8 December 2026 (renewal NIC scrutiny 6–30 November)</li>
</ul>
<p>So renewal payment is reported for <strong>15–22 December</strong>, not 7–11 December, and fresh payment from <strong>24 December</strong>, not 21 December. AKTU-affiliated colleges must submit the verified student list with the original affidavit by 28 November.</p>
</section><div class="note"><strong>Read these dates the right way:</strong> they are from the Social Welfare Department’s <strong>fourth revised timetable</strong> (20 November 2026), reported from the AKTU notice of 25 November 2026 by two sources (NotesGallery and AKTU Notes), and apply to AKTU-affiliated colleges. The official portal scholarship.up.gov.in has published no separate notice, and the AKTU notice PDF itself could not be opened, so this article does not call them officially announced — if any date changes, the portal is final. The form-closure and early-stage dates come from the third revised timetable (order dated 22 October 2026), which the fourth revision did not change.</div></section>
<section class="box"><h2>What each stage actually means</h2><p><strong>Institution and university verification.</strong> Your college first checks the form against your documents and forwards it; the university or affiliating agency then verifies that you are a genuine, enrolled student. A form stuck at either desk simply waits — it does not get rejected on its own, but it also cannot move ahead until that desk clears it.</p><p><strong>PFMS Aadhaar authentication.</strong> The payment for this scholarship goes through PFMS by DBT, so your Aadhaar is authenticated against the application and the bank account. If the name or date of birth in the form and in Aadhaar differ, this is the stage where the mismatch surfaces — which is why the details had to match from the start.</p><p><strong>District verification of suspicious data.</strong> Applications whose data was flagged — a mismatch in income, category, marks or bank details — are checked again at the district level. Most students will hear nothing in this stage; only flagged forms are examined closely.</p><p><strong>Demand generation and fund transfer.</strong> After verification closes, the department generates the payment demand and the fund transfer follows — under the fourth revised timetable, renewal payment is reported for 15–22 December 2026 and fresh payment for 24–31 December 2026. The amount reaches the Aadhaar-seeded bank account directly, with no agent in between. Payments for rectified applications are reported for January 2027 (renewal 16–25 January, fresh 27–31 January).</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>What you should do now</h2><ul class="checklist"><li><strong>Check your status on scholarship.up.gov.in:</strong> open “Status” with your application number and see which stage the form has reached — college, university, or beyond.</li><li><strong>Make sure the bank account is Aadhaar-seeded:</strong> the DBT payment goes only into an Aadhaar-linked account. If seeding is not done, visit the bank now — do not wait for December.</li><li><strong>If the college has not forwarded the form, go today:</strong> college forwarding ended on 26 November 2026. Take your application number and hard-copy receipt and ask the college where the form is stuck.</li><li><strong>Keep your documents ready:</strong> during district verification, a flagged form can require the income certificate, caste certificate, marksheet or bank details at short notice.</li><li><strong>Do not act on forwarded messages:</strong> dates are circulating on social media in many versions. The dates in this article are the reported fourth revised timetable — and scholarship.up.gov.in remains the final word.</li></ul><p>If a certificate behind your form needs checking — for example the income certificate number — verify it first with the <a href="/en/status-verification/">Status and Verification guide</a> before the district stage begins.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>If your status is stuck or your data is flagged</h2><p>A stuck status almost always has a desk behind it. If it shows pending with the college, the college is the first stop — carry the application number and the receipt of the hard copy you submitted. If it shows verified by the college but pending further, the university stage is due by 28 November for renewal and 30 November for fresh applicants, so ask the college whom to approach at the university. If your form is among the flagged ones, it will be examined during district verification — keep the original documents ready and respond quickly if the college or district asks for anything. Do not fill any “correction” form on an unofficial website; corrections, when they open, happen only on the official portal.</p></section>
<section class="box"><h2>Sources</h2><p>This article is based on the Social Welfare Department’s fourth revised timetable for UP Scholarship 2026-27 (20 November 2026), reported from the AKTU notice of 25 November 2026 by NotesGallery and AKTU Notes, for AKTU-affiliated colleges. The form-closure and early-stage dates come from the third revised timetable (order dated 22 October 2026; AKTU circular letter no. 14373 dated 31 October 2026), which the fourth revision did not change. The official portal scholarship.up.gov.in has published no separate notice on the fourth revision, and the AKTU notice PDF itself could not be opened — so these dates are reported, not officially announced. The earlier stages of this session are covered in our <a href="/en/blog/up-scholarship-verification-november-2026/">November verification schedule</a> article (the original schedule) and the <a href="/en/blog/up-scholarship-deadline-extension-13-november-2026/">deadline extension report</a>. No scholarship amounts or beneficiary figures are stated here, because the timetable does not fix them for an individual student — your amount depends on your category and course. If a date changes, scholarship.up.gov.in is final. For more guides, see the <a href="/en/">eDistrict UP homepage</a>.</p></section>
